-- title:
--   Kernel-ideal realisation of xg by an isogeny from W
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic a prime $q'$ which is algebraic over $\mathbb{Z}/q'$, let $X_1$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ all of whose $\kappa$-points killed by $q'$ are zero, and let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ satisfy $a<0$, $b<0$ and: for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division ring precisely when $q'\in v$. Let $\Lambda_1\subseteq\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is an order (contains $1$, is multiplicatively closed, spans over $\mathbb{Q}$, finitely generated) and is maximal among orders containing it, and let $\theta_1$ be an injective ring homomorphism from the subring of $\mathrm{End}(X_1(\kappa))$ generated by the $\kappa$-rational homomorphisms $X_1\to X_1$ onto $\Lambda_1$. Fix a unit $x$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$, an elliptic curve $W/\kappa$, a nonzero $\kappa$-rational $\chi:X_1\to W$ (an additive map on $\kappa$-points lying in `rationalHomSet`, i.e. zero or given off a finite set by fixed rational functions), and a unit $d$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, such that $\theta_1$ carries $\{\rho\circ\chi:\rho$ $\kappa$-rational $W\to X_1\}$ onto the image under quaternion conjugation of $d\cdot I_x$, where $I_y$ denotes the preimage in $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ of $y\cdot$`finiteAdeleBox`$\,\Lambda_1$ (the additive subgroup generated by the $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda_1$ and $\alpha$ an integral finite adele). Let $g$ be a unit lying in `finiteAdeleBox`$\,\Lambda_1$ and assume $q'$ does not divide the index of $I_{xg}$ relative to $I_x$. Then there are an elliptic curve $W'/\kappa$ and $\kappa$-rational additive maps $\psi:W\to W'$, $\psi':W'\to W$ with $\theta_1$ carrying $\{\rho\circ(\psi\circ\chi):\rho$ $\kappa$-rational $W'\to X_1\}$ onto the conjugate of $d\cdot I_{xg}$, and with $\psi'\circ\psi$ and $\psi\circ\psi'$ both equal to $n$ times the identity, $n=\#\ker\psi$.
--
--   This is the existence (lattice-to-subgroup) direction of Deuring's correspondence between left ideals of a maximal quaternion order and isogenies of supersingular elliptic curves, transported one level above the base curve $X_1$: shrinking the finite idele from $x$ to $xg$ by an amount prime to the characteristic is realised by an isogeny $\psi$ out of $W$, equipped with a dual isogeny. It feeds the construction of the bijection between ideal classes and supersingular points used in the Cerednik–Drinfeld description, being cited by [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_classSet_equiv_ssPlaces_forall_toValuationSubring_eq_comap_moduliPlace_ker`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_classSet_equiv_ssPlaces_forall_toValuationSubring_eq_comap_moduliPlace_ker) and by [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_equiv_ofFiniteIdele_mul_isAddCyclic_forall_ker_eq_of_kernelIdealSet_comp_eq`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_equiv_ofFiniteIdele_mul_isAddCyclic_forall_ker_eq_of_kernelIdealSet_comp_eq).
